/T (Greek economy collapsed because of high debt/GDP ratio. UK debt/GDP ratio was 69% in 2010 and forecast to increase to more than 100%. Austerity is crucial in promoting future economic growth and stability. Conservatives committed to increase public expenditure and cut taxes. Labour committed to public sector pay rises, green transformation fund, compensating WASPI women and building social housing. Low cost of borrowing. UK has a relatively low debt/GDP ratio. Destroys reputation of fiscal responsibility.)
